<p>About a month ago I moved and resized my work apps on my <a href="https://taonaw.com/2026/08/07/my-new-montior-is-pushing.html">big screen</a>, nodded to myself, and that was it. That&rsquo;s how they&rsquo;ve stayed. I never bothered organizing windows before, but these just clicked. It&rsquo;s only one specific work area: my left Space on my Mac, the one I keep for work. It contains:</p>
<ul>
<li>Microsoft Edge</li>
<li>Outlook</li>
<li>Teams</li>
<li>Emacs frame (of course)</li>
</ul>
<p>The right Space is reserved for personal things, and I don&rsquo;t have designated place for things there. That space only holds Safari and another frame of Emacs as a rule. Then there&rsquo;s a third app, like Discord if I&rsquo;m on it, or IDAGIO for music, or another program I opened.</p>
<p>This leaves my laptop&rsquo;s screen, bare besides Signal, which is how I chat with my partners and close friends. It stays on the same Space, so I see messages there no matter what. Lately I&rsquo;ve also started using it for Thunderbird, but not fully — if I want to write an email or read something longer, it migrates to the bigger, central screen.</p>
